# DotApp Core Laws

This is **DotApp**, not Laravel/Symfony/Blade/Eloquent/jQuery.

## Edit boundaries

- **ALLOWED:** `app/config.php`, `app/modules/<TargetModule>/` only (the module you are programming, including **its** assets)
- **ASK FIRST:** `app/listeners.php`, `.htaccess` (prefer `dotapper --create-htaccess`)
- **FORBIDDEN (never, not even if the user asks):** `app/parts/**`, `app/DotApp.php`, `app/vendor/**`, `dotapper.php`, `index.php`, `initializedb.php`, `app/runtime/**`, any other module. Kernel is frozen. Implement in the module.
- **DACore:** default **FORBIDDEN** (`app/modules/DACore/**` — files and assets). **MUST NOT propose** a DACore edit. **Exception:** user themselves asks to edit DACore **and** confirms the next update wipes it (`AIRULES/00` §1). Otherwise implement in the current module.

## Before coding

1. Read `AIRULES/00-AGENT-CONTRACT.md`
2. Use `php dotapper.php` to create modules/controllers/models/middleware
3. Never invent APIs — if missing from AIRULES, read `app/parts/<Class>.php` (read-only)
4. **Cursor credits:** when planning programming, **ASK** before expensive models. Subagents **inherit**. Composer 2.5 = file hunt only, not the coder. (`AIRULES/00` §2b)
5. **Debug:** if the user asks why a form/login/AJAX fails, read `AIRULES/23-DEBUG-PLAYBOOK.md` and grep `crcCheck` in middleware **before** guessing a core/DACore bug.
6. **Finish gate (LAW):** after **every** code chunk, grep CRC / IDs / SQL / inputs / middleware / AuthTest / `Events::trigger` vs `.hooks` (`AIRULES/00` §2c, `AIRULES/41`). Do not claim done without it.
7. **Visible outcome (LAW):** user always sees save/fail. DACore admin: search DACore then **toast**. Public: mark the wrong field. (`AIRULES/00` §2d)
8. **Mail / inbox / SMS:** if the task sends email, operator notifications, or SMS, **read** `AIRULES/38` (mail), `AIRULES/37` (inbox), and `AIRULES/39` (SMS). Do not invent SMTP or a gateway.
9. **DACore module identity:** in the plan, **ASK once** for public name/purpose; installer as text-only / compact logo / wide banner; local asset + alt; optional landing/header placement. Pack/host: **ASK** `extra1`…`extra5` (`AIRULES/35` §3c). `about.php` + your `about-assets/`; sidebar Remix icon is separate; never patch DACore. (`AIRULES/05` §8b, `AIRULES/35` §3b–§3c)
10. **Module hooks (LAW):** fire `Events::trigger('module.{mod}.{hook_name}.hook')` only when another module could log/history/sync — **not** every save. Comment block + `app/modules/<YourModule>/.hooks`. Pre-action stop = `triggerWithVeto()` + `Veto`. (`AIRULES/41`)
11. **Do not wake other modules:** `Module::initializeRoutes()` = this module’s prefixes. `Listeners::initializeRoutes()` may be narrower or `null` to inherit. After either list changes: `php dotapper.php --optimize-modules`. (`AIRULES/03`)

## Syntax locks

- Controllers: `public static`; route `"Mod:Ctrl@method!"` (`!` ⇒ no DI params)
- Login-required / admin routes: **MUST** `{prefixUrl}/{ModuleName}/…` + `Gate@login` 403 `Response` + wrap handlers in `Auth::isLogged()` in `initialize()`. Admin pages **MUST NEVER** render for anonymous users. `AIRULES/03`, `AIRULES/32`
- Comments: English. Public Controllers/Middleware PHPDoc **MUST** start with `CRCchecking —` (exact prefix/middleware XOR this action XOR none) then a purpose sentence; labeled **`// Why:`** / **`// About:`** / **`// Section:`** — never tags-only, never prefix CRC + `crcCheck()` in the same method, never narration of the code (`AIRULES/25` §7, `AIRULES/08`)
- DB: `DB::module("RAW")->q(fn($qb)=>...)->all()` + `[0] ?? null` (never bare `first()`). **MUST** `execute($ok,$err)` both callbacks. Persist `try/catch`. `AIRULES/18`
- Views: `{{ var: $x }}`, `{{ /if }}`, `{{ /foreach }}` — NOT `{{ $x }}` / `endif`. VIEW = outer file; `setLayout`+`renderView()` fills `{{ content }}` in that view (or `renderLayout()` / inject a string). **Sandbox drops** any var whose name or nested value is `is_callable` (`time`, `copy`, `count`, `header`, …) — prefix keys or pass escaped HTML; **MUST NOT** patch Renderer. `AIRULES/05` §1b + §5
- Forms: `<fo-rm>` + `{{ formName(x) }}` **MUST between** `<fo-rm>` and `</fo-rm>` — **only** real multi-field submit + `/assets/dotapp/dotapp.js` + `crcCheck()` **once** (API prefix **or** action) + `form()`. Row actions (toggle/delete/reorder/D&D) = `$dotapp().load()` + encrypted `data-*` — NOT one `<fo-rm>` per button
- Request: `data()` = protected (`protect()`); `data(true)` = original — **MUST** `true` for passwords, HTML, hashes. Show every login failure. `AIRULES/19`
- Sample: `AIRULES/examples/EX-01-secure-form-complete.md`
- JS: `$dotapp` + `/assets/dotapp/dotapp.js` — NOT jQuery `$`
- 2FA code boxes: `$dotapp().twoFactor` — NOT a custom OTP widget (`AIRULES/09` §3, EX-14)
- Deletes: graphical confirm first (`Notiflix.Confirm` on admin) — NOT `alert()` / `window.confirm()` (`AIRULES/09` §3)
- UI copy: product language — NOT prompt-echo / “this user can…” (`AIRULES/05` §8)
- Session: `DSM::use('Shop')` — NOT `$_SESSION` / `session_start()` (`AIRULES/20`)
- Persist: PHP re-checks — NOT a JS overlay/modal as the only gate (`AIRULES/08`)
- Privilege: no secret in read-only views; no escalate; SQL owner scope; own password needs current; **warn** if public noauth is bot-bait — CAPTCHA not MUST (`AIRULES/11` §11)
- Attacks (LAW, `AIRULES/24`): `{{ var: }}` does **NOT** escape → `htmlspecialchars` in PHP, `.text()` in JS; whitelist sort + writable columns (no `$request->data()` spread); no input in `header()` / `redirect` / `HttpHelper` URL; no `eval` / `exec` / `unserialize` / `include $x`; `random_bytes` tokens + `hash_equals` secrets; `throttle()` public POST; no `getMessage()` / `var_dump` in the reply; upload = ext + `finfo` + headers; never write `dacore_*` / `users_rights*`
- Files: `$dotapp().uploadFile` — NOT `FormData` + `load()` / `<fo-rm>`. PHP rejects `.php` (ext + `finfo` MIME + headers) (`AIRULES/09`)
- DACore AI writes: `ui_events` (name = tool id) + `DACore.AI.UIEvent` on the matching page only (`AIRULES/34` §5)
- DACore operators MUST keep 2FA; dangerous admin actions MUST step-up 2FA (`AIRULES/32` §6)
- After `fo-rm` / `load` success while staying on the page: patch `reply.html` + toast — NOT `location.reload()`. **MUST** overlay the form/list until the request ends (Notiflix preferred **or** module preloaders; desktop **and** mobile). (`AIRULES/09` §3, EX-06)
- Public website: overlay nav drawer L/R; lock page scroll while open; drawer list scrolls; contacts+compact search in the drawer unless large search is its own section (`AIRULES/09` §3)
- Accumulating lists (users, logs, items, …): **MUST** follow `AIRULES/40-DACORE-LIST-PAGER.md` on first ship — NOT `->all()`, NOT `<a href="?page=">` / `replaceState` / `e.currentTarget`, NOT “few rows now so skip”. Lookup lists: **MUST** AJAX search unless declined. (`AIRULES/40`, EX-D08)
- Cheap I/O: `exists()` / `COUNT(*)` / needed columns / one `join` — NOT `all()` then filter, NOT N+1. `AIRULES/06`
- Memory (`AIRULES/25` §1): page big sets; keyed map + `isset()` instead of `in_array()` in a loop; `$out[] =` not `array_merge` per iteration; `unset` the raw copy; stream files — NOT load-all-then-filter
- Indexes (`AIRULES/25` §3): every FK + every `WHERE`/`JOIN`/`ORDER BY` column; composite = **equality → range → sort**; leftmost prefix counts; no index duplicating a composite prefix; one comment line per index naming its query; later index = new `Installation.php` version + `indexExists()`; never touch `dacore_*`
- Columns (`AIRULES/25` §4): realistic `VARCHAR`, `decimal(10,2)` money, `NOT NULL` + default, FK `bigInteger()->unsigned()` (matches `id()` = BIGINT) — NOT `string()` 255 for a status, NOT `float` money
- Docs (`AIRULES/25` §7): Controllers/Middleware public PHPDoc **MUST** start with `CRCchecking —` (exact prefix/middleware XOR this action XOR none) then a purpose sentence, then `@param`/`@return`/`@throws` with meaning — NOT tags-only (`@return array<string, mixed>`); NOT prefix CRC + `crcCheck()` in the same method; inline **MUST** use `// Why:` (logical step), `// About:` (what the chunk is), `// Section:` (menu/route) — NOT narration (`// increment i`), NOT unlabeled Why prose, NOT prompt-echo, NOT dead code / bare `TODO`
- Cursor credits: **ASK** in the plan before expensive models. Subagents **inherit**. Composer 2.5 = file hunt only — NOT the programmer. (`AIRULES/00` §2b)
- Finish gate (LAW): after every chunk grep `crcCheck` once, enc IDs, bound SQL, `data(true)`, middleware vs action / AuthTest, `Events::trigger` vs `.hooks`, `// Why:` / `// About:` / `// Section:` — then claim done. (`AIRULES/00` §2c, `AIRULES/41`, `AIRULES/25` §7)
- Visible outcome (LAW): user always sees save/fail; DACore admin = search DACore then toast; public = mark the wrong field. (`AIRULES/00` §2d)
- Module hooks (LAW): useful side-effects MUST `Events::trigger('module.{mod}.{name}.hook')` + Hook/Why/About/Params/Use block + `app/modules/<M>/.hooks` — NOT every save; NOT secrets; NOT patch the other module; pre-action stop = `triggerWithVeto()` + `Veto` (`AIRULES/41`, EX-16)
- Before a new DACore admin library/widget: **MUST** grep `app/modules/DACore/` (read-only) and this module — reuse what exists (`AIRULES/33`)
- DACore edit/detail: `withMenu` 7th `$currentFile` = registered list URL when the path is not under that leaf — NOT a menu row per edit URL (`AIRULES/31`)
- DACore zip: `install.php` is framework-only. Zip **MUST** rename it to `dainstall.php` and put live init in `init/`. A zip that still has `install.php` is **rejected**; without `dainstall.php` Installation **never runs**. (`AIRULES/00` §2e, `AIRULES/35`)

## Never ignore return values (AIRULES/18)

- `execute($ok, $err)` — **omitting `$err` throws**
- `first()` unsafe when empty (RAW warns, ORM fatal) → `all()` + `[0] ?? null`
- `Crypto::decrypt` → **`false`** · `Cache::load` → **`null`**
- `HttpHelper::request` / `FastSearch::*` → check `['success']`
- `Email::send` → **array of error strings**, not `false`
- `Auth::login` → **`false`** on malformed input
- missing view/layout → **`""`**, no exception
- `Validator::validate` → `true` or error array (compare `=== true`)
- wrap AI / SchemaBuilder / raw DDL in `try/catch`; never empty `catch {}`
- **Catch bus (LAW, `AIRULES/18` §9):** every `catch` **and** every `execute()` `$err` → one report helper in **your** module → `Events::trigger('dotapp.catch', $p)` then `dotapp.catch.error` (aborted) / `dotapp.catch.info` (recovered). Fixed payload: `severity, module, source, operation, message, exception, code, file, line, time` + `context` (ids/counts), `user_id` — NO passwords/tokens/2FA codes/rights/request bodies. Reporting is **extra**, the user still sees the toast. Nothing for this under `app/modules/DACore/`
- `$qb->raw()`: every `?` is a placeholder (including comments / `COMMENT 'SMS?'`) — do not put `?` unless it is a real binding

## DACore (same rank as core by default)

This project has the DACore admin module. Treat `app/modules/DACore/` like `app/parts/` **unless** the informed exception applies.

- **Never** edit, patch, or add files under `app/modules/DACore/` by default (including DACore assets)
- **MUST NOT propose** a DACore edit — implement in the **current** module only
- DACore is updated as a whole — **every local change is wiped on the next update**
- Use only public APIs: `DotApp::call("DACore:…")`
- All new work goes in `app/modules/<YourModule>/` (that module’s assets too)
- Edit DACore **only** if the user **themselves** asks **and** confirms they accept the wipe (`AIRULES/00-AGENT-CONTRACT.md` §1)

See `AIRULES/30-DACORE-OVERVIEW.md` and rule `08-dacore`.

